{"name":"Pale Sagebrush","hex":"#d3d1b9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pale","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Light in color.","Having a pallor (a light color, especially due to sickness, shock, fright etc.)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To turn pale; to lose colour.","To become insignificant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pale"},{"term":"sagebrush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several North American aromatic shrubs of the genus Artemisia, having silvery-grey, green leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sagebrush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sagebrush","blocks":[{"text":"Sagebrush is the common name of several woody and herbaceous species of plants in the genus Artemisia. The best-known sagebrush is the shrub Artemisia tridentata. Sagebrush is native to the western half of North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Sagebrushsjc.jpg/330px-Sagebrushsjc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sagebrush","wikidata":"Q7399162"},{"title":"Colorfulness","blocks":[{"text":"Colorfulness, chroma and saturation are attributes of perceived color relating to chromatic intensity. As defined formally by the International Commission on Illumination (CIE) they respectively describe three different aspects of chromatic intensity, but the terms are often used loosely and interchangeably in contexts where these aspects are not clearly distinguished. The precise meanings of the terms vary by what other functions they are dependent on."},{"items":["Colorfulness is the \"attribute of a visual perception according to which the perceived color of an area appears to be more or less chromatic \". The colorfulness evoked by an object depends not only on its spectral reflectance but also on the strength of the illumination, and increases with the latter unless the brightness is very high.","Chroma is the \"colorfulness of an area judged as a proportion of the brightness of a similarly illuminated area that appears white or highly transmitting\". As a result, chroma is mostly only dependent on the spectral properties, and as such is seen to describe the object color. It is how different from a grey of the same lightness such an object color appears to be.","Saturation is the \"colorfulness of an area judged in proportion to its brightness\", which in effect is the perceived freedom from whitishness of the light coming from the area. An object with a given spectral reflectance exhibits approximately constant saturation for all levels of illumination, unless the brightness is very high."]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Brightness_and_colorfulness.png/330px-Brightness_and_colorfulness.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colorfulness","wikidata":"Q27673"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Artemisia_tridentata_2.jpg/500px-Artemisia_tridentata_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Artemisia_tridentata_2.jpg/1280px-Artemisia_tridentata_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Artemisia_tridentata_2.jpg/500px-Artemisia_tridentata_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Leaves and flowers of Artemisia tridentata","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArtemisia_tridentata_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Artemisia_pygmaea.jpg/330px-Artemisia_pygmaea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Artemisia_pygmaea.jpg/330px-Artemisia_pygmaea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artemisia pygmaea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArtemisia_pygmaea.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Saturation_of_digital_colors.png/500px-Saturation_of_digital_colors.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Saturation_of_digital_colors.png/500px-Saturation_of_digital_colors.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"7.5PB and 10BG Munsell hue pages of RGB colors, showing lines of uniform saturation (chroma in proportion to lightness) in red. Lines of uniform saturation radiate from near the black point, while lines of uniform chroma are vertical. Also compared to the 10BG colors, the 7.5PB colors attain higher saturation as well as higher chroma.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaturation_of_digital_colors.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Surfing_in_Hawaii_unmodified.jpg/500px-Surfing_in_Hawaii_unmodified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Surfing_in_Hawaii_unmodified.jpg/500px-Surfing_in_Hawaii_unmodified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASurfing_in_Hawaii_unmodified.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Surfing_in_Hawaii%2B50_LCh_chroma.jpg/500px-Surfing_in_Hawaii%2B50_LCh_chroma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Surfing_in_Hawaii%2B50_LCh_chroma.jpg/500px-Surfing_in_Hawaii%2B50_LCh_chroma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","al